{%- comment -%}
  GOD SQUAD — Product media gallery
  Phase 8.

  Accepts:
  - product    {Object}  required.
  - section_id {String}  required. Namespaces every id on the page.
  - layout     {String}  optional, 'stacked' (default) or 'carousel'.
  - sizes      {String}  optional. The sizes attribute for the media. The
                         section owns the grid, so the section computes it.

  Usage:
  {% render 'product-media-gallery', product: product, section_id: section.id %}

  EVERY MEDIUM IS REACHABLE WITH JAVASCRIPT OFF.
  The brief's rule — "All actual product media must remain accessible. Do not
  display only the first image if additional product media exists" — is met
  structurally rather than by script. Every medium is in the DOM at full size;
  the two layouts are a CSS switch over one markup:

    stacked   the media run down the column and the customer scrolls. This is
              the editorial default and needs no script at all.
    carousel  one frame at a time in a scroll-snap scroller. Native scrolling
              and swiping still work with no script; the thumbnail rail is a
              list of in-page anchors, so it works too.

  There is no carousel library, no slider, and nothing about buying this
  product depends on this file's behaviour.

  MEDIA IS product.media, NOT product.images.
  images cannot represent a video or a 3D model, and a variant's featured_image
  cannot either — only featured_media can. Dispatching on media_type is what
  lets the four Shopify types render correctly, with an else arm so a type
  added later still draws rather than vanishing.

  LOADING.
  The first medium is the page's largest above-the-fold image and is the LCP
  candidate: loading eager, fetchpriority high. Everything after it is lazy.
  Phase 2 §14.6 and the brief agree — "do NOT blindly lazy-load every product
  image", and equally do not eagerly load six of them.

  OBJECT-POSITION IS SHOPIFY'S.
  image_tag writes an inline object-position onto the img from the image's
  focal point, and an inline style beats any rule in a stylesheet. The frames
  below therefore crop with object-fit and leave the position alone, and no
  style: parameter is passed to image_tag. This is the same finding Phase 7
  recorded for the story band.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign gallery_layout = layout | default: 'stacked'
  assign media_items = product.media
  assign media_count = media_items.size

  comment
    The medium the page opens on. A variant carries featured_media when the
    merchant has assigned one; when it has not, the first medium leads. Matched
    on id rather than position, because position is nil for media sourced from
    a metafield.
  endcomment
  assign active_media_id = product.selected_or_first_available_variant.featured_media.id

  comment
    The slot the image occupies. The caller knows the grid and computes it;
    the fallback is the honest shape of the same thing for a caller that does
    not, and is never what the product section uses.
  endcomment
  assign media_sizes = sizes | default: '(min-width: 1024px) calc((100vw - 128px) * 0.64), 100vw'
-%}

{%- if media_count > 0 -%}
  <div
    class="product-gallery product-gallery--{{ gallery_layout }}"
    data-product-gallery
    data-gallery-layout="{{ gallery_layout }}"
  >
    <div class="product-gallery__viewport" data-gallery-viewport>
      {%- for media in media_items -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign is_active = false
          if active_media_id != blank
            if media.id == active_media_id
              assign is_active = true
            endif
          elsif forloop.first
            assign is_active = true
          endif

          assign slide_id = section_id | append: '-media-' | append: media.id
        -%}
        <div
          class="product-gallery__slide{% if is_active %} is-active{% endif %}"
          id="{{ slide_id }}"
          data-media-id="{{ media.id }}"
          data-media-type="{{ media.media_type }}"
        >
          <div class="product-gallery__frame">
            {%- case media.media_type -%}
              {%- when 'image' -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  PHASE 16: is_active, NOT forloop.first.

                  The slide the page opens on is the active one — the variant's
                  featured media when it has one (see is_active above, which
                  falls back to forloop.first when it does not). Keying the
                  eager load and fetchpriority to forloop.first meant that on
                  any product whose selected variant is not the first medium,
                  the browser was told to hurry an image nobody was looking at
                  and to lazy-load the LCP element.

                  forloop.first still gets loading: eager, because the stacked
                  desktop layout renders every slide in document order and the
                  first one is on screen there regardless. Only ONE image gets
                  fetchpriority, and it is the active one.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- if is_active -%}
                  {{
                    media
                    | image_url: width: 1800
                    | image_tag:
                      class: 'product-gallery__image',
                      widths: '360, 480, 640, 800, 960, 1200, 1400, 1600, 1800',
                      sizes: media_sizes,
                      loading: 'eager',
                      fetchpriority: 'high',
                      decoding: 'async',
                      alt: media.alt
                  }}
                {%- elsif forloop.first -%}
                  {{
                    media
                    | image_url: width: 1800
                    | image_tag:
                      class: 'product-gallery__image',
                      widths: '360, 480, 640, 800, 960, 1200, 1400, 1600, 1800',
                      sizes: media_sizes,
                      loading: 'eager',
                      decoding: 'async',
                      alt: media.alt
                  }}
                {%- else -%}
                  {{
                    media
                    | image_url: width: 1800
                    | image_tag:
                      class: 'product-gallery__image',
                      widths: '360, 480, 640, 800, 960, 1200, 1400, 1600, 1800',
                      sizes: media_sizes,
                      loading: 'lazy',
                      decoding: 'async',
                      alt: media.alt
                  }}
                {%- endif -%}

              {%- when 'video' -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  Shopify-hosted video. video_tag needs no script of its own.
                  Controls are on and autoplay is off: an autoplaying product
                  video is motion the customer did not ask for, which Phase 2
                  §21.5 rules out, and it costs a stranger on a phone data they
                  did not choose to spend.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {{ media | video_tag: class: 'product-gallery__video', controls: true, preload: 'metadata', image_size: '1200x' }}

              {%- when 'external_video' -%}
                {{ media | external_video_url: autoplay: false | external_video_tag: class: 'product-gallery__video', loading: 'lazy' }}

              {%- when 'model' -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  A 3D model renders as inert markup until the theme calls
                  Shopify.loadFeatures for model-viewer-ui, and augmented
                  reality needs a second, independent call. No God Squad
                  product carries a model today, so the loader is not shipped
                  and this arm renders the static preview Shopify supplies
                  instead of an element that would never initialise. Recorded
                  as a known limitation rather than half-built.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- if media.preview_image != blank -%}
                  {{
                    media.preview_image
                    | image_url: width: 1800
                    | image_tag:
                      class: 'product-gallery__image',
                      widths: '360, 480, 640, 800, 960, 1200, 1400, 1600, 1800',
                      sizes: media_sizes,
                      loading: 'lazy',
                      decoding: 'async',
                      alt: media.alt
                  }}
                {%- endif -%}

              {%- else -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  A media type added to Shopify after this was written. It
                  renders through the generic filter rather than disappearing.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {{ media | media_tag: class: 'product-gallery__media' }}
            {%- endcase -%}
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

    {%- if media_count > 1 -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The rail. Anchors, not buttons: with no script an anchor still brings
        its slide into view, and it is keyboard-operable for free. The script
        cancels the jump so no history entry is created — the brief asks that
        browsing media not fill the back button — and scrolls smoothly instead.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <nav class="product-gallery__rail" aria-label="{{ 'products.media.rail_label' | t }}" data-gallery-rail>
        <ul class="product-gallery__thumbs" role="list">
          {%- for media in media_items -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign is_active = false
              if active_media_id != blank
                if media.id == active_media_id
                  assign is_active = true
                endif
              elsif forloop.first
                assign is_active = true
              endif
              assign slide_id = section_id | append: '-media-' | append: media.id
            -%}
            <li class="product-gallery__thumb-item">
              <a
                class="product-gallery__thumb{% if is_active %} is-active{% endif %}"
                href="#{{ slide_id }}"
                data-gallery-thumb
                data-media-id="{{ media.id }}"
                {% if is_active %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}
              >
                {%- if media.preview_image != blank -%}
                  {{
                    media.preview_image
                    | image_url: width: 240
                    | image_tag:
                      class: 'product-gallery__thumb-image',
                      widths: '80, 120, 160, 240',
                      sizes: '80px',
                      loading: 'lazy',
                      decoding: 'async',
                      alt: ''
                  }}
                {%- endif -%}
                <span class="visually-hidden">
                  {{- 'products.media.go_to' | t: index: forloop.index, count: media_count -}}
                  {%- unless media.media_type == 'image' -%}
                    {{ ' ' }}{{ media.media_type }}
                  {%- endunless -%}
                </span>
              </a>
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      </nav>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- else -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    No media on the product. The frame still draws so the page keeps its
    proportions, and nothing stands in for a photograph that does not exist.
    Phase 3 records production product photography as still outstanding.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="product-gallery product-gallery--empty">
    <div class="product-gallery__frame product-gallery__frame--empty" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
